# filename: .gitignore
# title: Version-Control Ignore List
# description:
#     Tells Git which files and folders must never be committed to the
#     merged VEDA repository. Every pattern here is deliberate. Do not
#     remove an entry without knowing why it was added.
#
# source:
#     AUTHORED — veda's repo had no committed .gitignore, and the
#     personal prototype's .gitignore was not uploaded. This list is
#     built from standard Python practice plus the specific rules
#     required by this project.
#
# notes:
#     - The most important entry is ".env". The personal prototype's
#       .env file contains a real email address and must never be
#       committed. The template ".env.example" IS committed; it holds
#       placeholders only.
#     - The archive/ folders intentionally DO get committed. They
#       contain the two original prototypes as read-only references.
#       Their own .venv/ and .env files, if present, are excluded by
#       the patterns below.

# --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and local configuration
# --------------------------------------------------------------------
# The real .env file holds SEC_API_USER_AGENT (name + email) and any
# future secrets. It is per-developer and must never be committed.
# .env.example is the committed template and is NOT ignored.
.env
*.env
!.env.example

# --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python virtual environments
# --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Any virtual environment created inside the project. Excluded so the
# repository does not carry thousands of installed package files.
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python bytecode and caches
# --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated at import time. Never source. Recreated automatically.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class

# --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Packaging and build artefacts
# --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Produced by pip install -e . and by building a distribution. Never
# committed.
*.egg-info/
*.egg
build/
dist/
.eggs/

# --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test and tool caches
# --------------------------------------------------------------------
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.tox/

# --------------------------------------------------------------------
# IDE and OS files
# --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor-specific directories. Not source.
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/launch.json
!.vscode/settings.json
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local output
# --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Files written by the CLI's --output flag, and any local scratch
# JSON. Not part of the repository. Named with a leading underscore
# or explicitly matched.
*.local.json
_output/
packet.json
test_run.txt
failures.txt